	"roles": {
		"netmender": {"title": "Net-mender", "work": "nets",
			"intro": ["Mind the nets. Every hole you step through, I mend twice.", "{name}. I mend what the sea tears. Lately that's everything."],
			"self": ["My father mended nets, and his mother before him. I tried farming once. The yams laughed at me.",
				"A net's only holes held together with string. Same as a village, if you think about it. Don't think about it."],
			"talk": ["The sea took a bite out of my best net last night. Left the fish, kept the knots.",
				"Salt in the twine, sun on the twine. Twine never gets a day off. Neither do I.",
				"I can tell what tore a net by the hole. This one? Something with teeth and opinions.",
				"Mending's quiet work. You hear the waves, the gulls, and everyone else's business.",
				"Rain's good for nets. Softens the cord. Bad for my fingers, but the nets come first.",
				"Some days I think the fish are cutting the nets themselves. Clever little thieves.",
				"Bring me a net off your ship sometime. I'll show you what a proper knot looks like."]},
		"hunter": {"title": "Hunter", "work": "forage",
			"intro": ["You walk loud for a pirate. Good. The jungle likes to know who's coming.", "{name}. I hunt. Pigs, mostly. Bugs, when they come looking."],
			"self": ["I've tracked everything on this island except the thing on the far side. That one tracks me.",
				"Two of my brothers went to the high ground last season. One came back. He doesn't hunt any more."],
			"talk": ["Pig tracks by the creek this morning. Big boar. He's been laughing at me all season.",
				"Wind's wrong today. Everything in the bush can smell me coming. Even the bugs.",
				"You learn to read the mud out here. Mud never lies. Hunters do, all the time.",
				"Heat makes the pigs lazy and the bugs angry. I'd rather hunt pigs, so I go early.",
				"I sharpen my spear every night. Not for pigs. For whatever's been following my trail.",
				"The pirates in the bush scare off the game. Loud boots, loud fires, loud everything.",
				"Last week I followed a trail for two days. It led me home. The jungle has a sense of humour."]},
		"healer": {"title": "Healer", "work": "home",
			"intro": ["Sit, if you're bleeding. Stand, if you're not. I'm busy.", "I'm {name}. Leaves for fever, mud for stings, rum for everything else."],
			"self": ["Half my cures are leaves and the other half is telling people to stop doing what hurts.",
				"I learned from the old healer, who learned from the ruins. The carvings there aren't all about war."],
			"talk": ["Three stings, a broken toe and a fever, and it's not even noon. Busy jungle.",
				"The rains bring fevers. The fevers bring people to my door. I'd rather the rains stayed away.",
				"Bug bites itch worse if you scratch. Everybody scratches. Nobody listens to me.",
				"I'm short on the red leaf. It only grows by the ruins, and nobody wants to fetch it.",
				"Pirates come to me too, when they're bleeding enough. A wound doesn't pick sides. Neither do I.",
				"If you get bitten by something with more than eight legs, come straight here. Run, ideally."]},
		"carver": {"title": "Carver", "work": "market",
			"intro": ["Every paddle in this village came off my knee. Most of the masts too.", "{name}. Carver. If it's wood and it's useful, I made it."],
			"self": ["I carved an idol for every ship that left here. Some of them even came back.",
				"Ironwood, from the hills. It blunts a knife in an afternoon. It also stops a cutlass."],
			"talk": ["This paddle's been fighting me all morning. The grain runs crooked, like its owner.",
				"Wet season swells the wood. Dry season cracks it. Carving's mostly arguing with weather.",
				"My chisels are older than half this village, and sharper than all of it.",
				"Somebody wants a new canoe by the feast. I want a nap. We'll see who wins.",
				"I keep the shavings. They light the plaza fire. Nothing goes to waste on a little island.",
				"Carved a figurehead once that looked so fierce, the owner wouldn't sail behind it."]},
		"storyteller": {"title": "Storyteller", "work": "plaza",
			"intro": ["Another captain! Sit. I'll tell you how the last one died. It's a good one.", "Old {name}. I keep the stories. Someone has to, and my knees won't let me do anything else."],
			"self": ["I've told the story of the first canoe a thousand times. It's longer every time. So is the canoe.",
				"When I was young the beast was a story for children. Now the children tell it to me."],
			"talk": ["Every story here starts with the sea and ends with the jungle. The middle's where it gets good.",
				"The children want stories about the beast. Their mothers want stories about anything else.",
				"My voice goes hoarse in the rains. Then I tell the short ones. Nobody likes the short ones.",
				"I'm working on a story about you, Captain. It has no ending yet. Try to give it a good one.",
				"My memory's going. Lucky for me, my stories got better without it.",
				"The old stones have a story too. I've never heard it all. Nobody living has."]},
		"watcher": {"title": "Lookout", "work": "nets",
			"intro": ["Saw your sails at dawn. Didn't ring the bell. You didn't look like the bell sort.", "{name}. I watch the sea. Someone's got to see the trouble before it lands."],
			"self": ["Three kinds of sail come past here: traders, pirates, and the ones that don't come back. I can tell them apart at a league.",
				"My eyes are the best on the island. My knees are the worst. The lookout on the summit was built for me, then they built the stairs."],
			"talk": ["Clear sky, flat sea, three gulls fighting over a crab. Exciting day up here.",
				"Smoke in the bush this morning. Pirate cookfire. They burn green wood, the fools.",
				"Squall coming in from the east by dusk. Tie down anything you love.",
				"I count canoes out and canoes back. Every day the numbers match is a good day.",
				"Long days on watch. I talk to the gulls. Lately they've started answering.",
				"A ship drifted past last month with nobody at the helm. I'm still watching for whoever it lost."]},
		"brewer": {"title": "Brewer", "work": "market",
			"intro": ["Thirsty? Course you are. You've got that sea-salt look.", "{name}. I brew the palm wine. The innkeeper takes the credit."],
			"self": ["Palm sap, sun and patience. Two of those are free.", "A pirate once offered me a ship for my recipe. I gave him a jug instead. He's still out there somewhere, happy."],
			"talk": ["This batch needs three more days in the sun. The innkeeper needs it yesterday.",
				"Climbing palms for sap at my age. The trees are winning, but slowly.",
				"Bugs love palm wine more than sailors do. I spend half the day swatting.",
				"A good brew tastes like sunshine with a kick. A bad one just kicks.",
				"Rain thins the sap. Thin sap, thin wine, thin tempers at the inn.",
				"I tried brewing fruit once. The pigs got into it. Best night that pig ever had."]},
	},
	"barks": {
		"day": ["Hot one today. They're all hot ones.", "The fruit's late this year. Everything's late this year.", "Watch the red ants. They don't watch you back, they just bite.",
			"Ships come, ships go. Most of them come back lighter.", "Don't drink from the green pools. Trust me.", "You're a long way from the sea up here. Well. Nobody's far from the sea here.",
			"Morning rain, noon steam, evening rain. That's the forecast. Always.", "Fresh coconuts by the gate, if you can crack them.",
			"Mind the vines on the path. Some of them aren't vines.", "My shirt hasn't been dry since the day I was born.",
			"A pirate! A real one? Show us your scar, then.", "The parrots are loud today. Means rain, or means parrots.",
			"Bananas are in. Mind the spiders in the bunches.", "Lovely day for sailing. Shame I'm stuck weeding.",
			"The pirates up the hill shot at a parrot all morning. The parrot won.", "Somebody left the gate open. Now there's a pig in the shrine.",
			"Too hot to work, too hot to sleep. Just right for complaining.", "Saw your ship come in. Fine lines. Who's your carver?",
			"Keep your boots on. The sand bites back at midday."],
		"evening": ["The inn's the only place the bugs won't follow you.", "Another day the jungle didn't eat us. Drink to that.", "Sun's going. Keep to the lamps.",
			"Listen. Hear that? That's the jungle waking up.", "Sky's going red. Red sky, wet morning. Every morning's wet.",
			"Fireflies out already. Pretty, till they land in your soup.", "Lamps are lit. Bugs are coming. Same as every night.",
			"Work's done. Well. Work's stopped. It's never done.", "Smell that? Fish on the coals at the plaza.",
			"The frogs start up about now. They don't stop till dawn.", "Get your canoe up the beach before the tide does it for you.",
			"Cooler now. Cool enough to sweat a little less.", "My feet ache. My back aches. Palm wine fixes both, briefly.",
			"Evening's the best part. Too dark to work, too early to worry.", "Children! In! Before the dark gets you!",
			"Bats are out over the water. Means the fish are rising.", "One more drink, then home. That's what I said yesterday.",
			"Quick, wash up before the cook blows the shell for supper.", "The day's heat stays in the stones a while. Sit on them. Lovely."],
		"night": ["Keep to the paths after dark. The trees have eyes, and some of them are hungry.", "Can't sleep. Something big walking about on the far side.",
			"Shh. If you can hear it, it can hear you.", "Who's there? Oh. You. Thought you were something with more legs.",
			"Out late, Captain? The jungle doesn't sleep. Neither should you, then.", "Stars are bright tonight. The beast's quiet. Both good signs.",
			"Bar the door, my mother said. Then she went out drinking.", "That rustling? Probably a pig. Probably.",
			"Moon's up. Good. I like seeing what's looking at me.", "I keep a lamp lit all night. The bugs think it's a party.",
			"The pirate camp's drums go till the moon sets. Nobody here sleeps much.", "Don't go near the ruins at night. The stones get cold. Stones shouldn't.",
			"Rain at night is the jungle breathing. Big, wet breaths.", "My dog won't stop growling at the far hills. Good dog.",
			"The fire's low and nobody wants to fetch wood. Not out there.", "Watch your step. The crabs come up the paths in the dark.",
			"Late for a walk. Early for trouble. Go to bed, Captain.", "Something howled out past the gardens. Then it stopped. Stopping is worse."],
		"nets": ["Fish are running deep. The beast's got them scared too.", "Hand me that float. No, the other float.", "Every knot's a prayer. Most of them hold.",
			"Pull, then. Gently. It's a net, not an anchor.", "Something big went through this one. Look at the size of that hole.",
			"Morning catch was good. The afternoon catch is mostly weed.", "Mind your boots on the twine. It's wet, it's slippery, and it's mine."],
		"forage": ["Mushrooms here. Don't eat the blue ones.", "Bug tracks. Fresh. Keep your voice down.", "Good roots under this one. Help me dig, or move on.",
			"Wild ginger. Smell it? Better than any rum.", "These berries are sweet. Those ones will kill you. Learn which fast.",
			"Quiet. Pig rooting just past those ferns.", "My basket's half full and my arms are all bitten."],
		"dock": ["Tide's turning. Everything's late when the tide turns.", "Mind the ropes. Mind the planks. Mind yourself, mostly.", "Your ship? She sits low. Carrying something heavy, or just tired?",
			"Unloading's done by noon, or it's done in the rain.", "Crates off the trader's ship. They smell of pepper and trouble.",
			"Tie off proper, Captain. The swell comes in sideways here.", "The pier creaks, but it's held for forty years. Don't jump."],
		"boats": ["Every canoe here came off this beach. Most of them came back to it.", "Hand me that adze. No, the sharp one. They're all sharp. That one.",
			"This hull needs pitch. Everything needs pitch, eventually.", "Outrigger's cracked. Again. The reef doesn't forgive.",
			"Want to race? My canoe against your ship. Around the point.", "Turn her over gently. A canoe remembers rough hands.",
			"Paddled out past the reef at dawn. Sea was glass. Fish were gone."],
		"stall": ["Fresh this morning. Well. This morning somewhere.", "Fish, rope, rum. The three things a sailor can't do without, in no order.",
			"Dried fish, two for a coin. Three if you stop sniffing them.", "Sea salt, scraped off the rocks myself. Finest on the island.",
			"Fishhooks! Sharp enough to catch a sea king. A small one.", "Look, don't touch. Touch, and you've bought it.",
			"The trader's ship took all my good stock. This is the rest."],
		"market": ["Shells, fruit, a fish that only smells a bit. What d'you need?", "Prices go up when ships come in. That's you. Sorry.", "Haggle all you like. I'm deaf on that side.",
			"Mangoes! Ripe today, rotten tomorrow, so buy now.", "Woven mats, fine as silk, tough as a pirate's hide.",
			"Pepper from the hills. Clears your head and your nose.", "No credit, no tabs, no pirates' promises."],
		"home": ["Roof's leaking again. The roof's always leaking.", "The little ones are down at the beach. I hope.", "If you see a pig with one ear, it's mine.",
			"Sweeping out the sand. It comes back. It always comes back.", "The thatch needs redoing before the big rains.",
			"Supper's yams again. It's always yams.", "Had a lizard move into the rafters. He eats the bugs. He stays."],
		"plaza": ["Gather round, gather round. No? Fine.", "The fire's never gone out. Not once. Not since my grandmother's grandmother.", "Elder's in a mood. Elder's always in a mood.",
			"Feast's in three days. Somebody tell the pigs to hide.", "Dance tonight, if the rain holds off. It won't.",
			"News from the boats! None. But I like shouting it.", "The drums need new skins. The old ones are mostly hole."],
		"inn": ["Pull up a stump. Seats are for paying folk.", "This round's on whoever's last to the bar. That's you.", "To the captains! May they pay their tabs.",
			"Palm wine, fresh today. Well. Fresh this week.", "Mind that bench. One leg's shorter than the rest. Like me.",
			"Somebody sing! Not you. You, the other one.", "Best place on the island to dry off and get wet again."],
		"workshop": ["Saw's dull. Everything's dull. Except the splinters.", "Mind the shavings. They'll stick to you for a week.",
			"Ironwood again. My arms are going to fall off.", "Measure twice, cut once, swear at it a third time.",
			"That stool's for sale. That one's for sitting. Don't mix them up.", "New keel for the big canoe. Smell that wood. Sweet as fruit.",
			"Glue's drying. Don't breathe on it. Don't look at it hard either."],
		"field": ["Weeds grow twice as fast as yams. I've measured.", "Wash day. The sun's out. Quick, before it changes its mind.",
			"Taro's coming up nicely. The pigs have noticed too.", "Pick a row and pull weeds, or stop standing on my beans.",
			"Laundry's been on the line three days. Still damp. It's the jungle.", "Those birds eat more of my garden than I do.",
			"Dig, plant, pray for sun, get rain. Gardening."],
		"shrine": ["Leave a flower for the old ones. They like the red ones.", "Quiet here. Even the bugs keep their voices down.",
			"I asked the spirits for rain once. I've regretted it ever since.", "Somebody left a jug of palm wine as an offering. Somebody else drank it.",
			"These stones came from the ruins. Older than the village. Older than the trees.", "A prayer for the fishers, a prayer for the hunters, one for me."],
		"well": ["Water's sweet this week. Last week it tasted of frog.", "Bucket's on the hook. Bring it back full or don't bring it back.",
			"Lean over and shout. The echo shouts back rude things.", "Deep well, cold water. Best thing in all this heat.",
			"Somebody dropped a sandal down there. Nobody's admitting it.", "Queue's long today. Everyone's thirsty when the rain stops."],
		"bench": ["Sit, Captain. Bench holds two. Three if one's small.", "I'm resting. Been resting since breakfast. Hard work.",
			"Did you hear about the brewer's pig? No? Sit down.", "Best seat on the island. You see everyone, and everyone sees you.",
			"My grandson thinks he'll be a pirate. I told him to start with dishes.", "Watching the sea costs nothing. Best show there is.",
			"That one over there owes me three fish and an apology."],
		"storehouse": ["Sacks of taro, stacked to the roof. Don't sneeze.", "Lift with your legs. That crate's heavier than it looks. Everything is.",
			"Dry season stores. Keep the rats out, keep the rain out, keep the pirates out.", "Count it again. One sack short. Somebody's been snacking.",
			"Rope, salt, smoked fish, a broken oar. Don't ask about the oar.", "Haul the jars to the back. Gently. Palm wine bruises."],
		"pointer": ["If you're after work, {who} {where} has been muttering about something all week.", "{who}'s got a problem. {who} always has a problem. This one sounded real.",
			"Go and see {who} {where}. Nobody listens to {who}, and that's never ended well.", "Ask {who} {where}. They've been pacing like a pig in a pen.",
			"{who} {where} needs a hand, and I've only got two, both busy.", "Looking for trouble? {who} has plenty to spare. Try {where}.",
			"Talk to {who}. Something's wrong and they won't tell me what.", "Heard {who} {where} offering coin for help. Real coin, not shells.",
			"You'd do us all a kindness seeing {who} {where}. Before the sulking starts.", "{who} came back from the jungle white as salt. Go and ask why.",
			"There's {who}, {where}. Strong arms like yours could help.", "Somebody should check on {who} {where}. Not me. I'm busy. You, then.",
			"Word is {who} wants a pirate for a job. You're a pirate, aren't you?"],
	},
	"menu": ["What is it, Captain?", "Captain. You need something?", "Oh! You startled me. What can I do for you?",
		"Speak up, Captain. The bugs are louder than you.", "Make it quick. The heat's eating my day.", "A pirate at my elbow. Should I be worried?",
		"Yes? I've a minute. Maybe two.", "Captain! Come to chat, or come to ask for something?", "Out with it. Whatever it is, it's been a long day already.",
		"Well, look who it is. What brings you over?", "You've got a question face on. Go on, then."],
	"work_menu": "So how's the work going, then? Jungle treating you all right?",
	"bye": "Goodbye.",
	"rumour_menu": ["What's the word on this island?", "Heard anything about the islands ahead?"],
	# (by the kind of POI they're about, {name} the POI's own; "any" fits whatever the island has)
	"rumour_isle": {
		"camp": ["They say {name} buried something in the jungle before setting up camp. They also say {name} can't count, so who knows how deep.",
			"{name}'s crew raid the gardens on moonless nights. Fat lot of good that does them. Nothing grows here but bugs."],
		"beast": ["{name} came down from the high ground three moons ago. It doesn't eat people. It just doesn't like them.",
			"Nobody goes to the far side any more. {name} broke the trees there like kindling. Big as a hut, the hunters say, and smart."],
		"lair": ["The bugs in the burrows hum before rain. Louder every year. One day it'll rain bugs, mark me."],
		"ruins": ["The old stones were here before the first canoe. Whoever built them left in a hurry, or didn't leave at all."],
		"lookout": ["Climb to the lookout on the summit on a clear day and you'll see three islands. On a bad day you'll see one, and it's this one."],
		"any": ["Something's not right out at {name}. Nobody says what. Nobody goes to look, either.", "My uncle went to {name} once. Came back with a story and no shoes. Still won't say which he values more."],
	},
	"rumour_chain": [
		"Canoes that make it to {name} come back quiet. {blurb}, they say, and meaner than here.",
		"A trader swore {name} has more gold than people. Then he went back, and now it has one more person.",
		"The needle pulls toward {name} next. {blurb}. Pack warm, or pack light, depending.",
		"I've a cousin on {name}. Haven't heard from her in a year. That's normal for her. Probably.",
	],
	"rumour_quiet": ["Quiet island, this. Too quiet, my mother says, but she says that about everything.",
		"Rumours? Nothing worth your ears. The yams are late. That's the big news.",
		"Can't say I've heard a thing. The jungle keeps its secrets, and so do I.",
		"Nothing new. Same bugs, same heat, same pirates up the hill.",
		"If there's word going round, it hasn't come round to me.",
		"Ask the storyteller. Whatever they haven't heard, they make up.",
		"Not a whisper this week. Even the gossips are short of gossip.",
		"Honestly? Nothing. I've been too busy to listen."],
	"rumour_fork":"The sea splits past here: {a}, or {b}. Pick one. The other's never as good as you'd hoped.",
	"rumour_end": "Past us? Nothing, the old ones say. The sea just ends, and something waits at the edge of it.",
	"rumour_hard": "Harder country than this, mind. Their bugs eat our bugs.",
	"self_menu": "Tell me about yourself.",
	"accept": "I'll see to it.",
	"decline": "Not now.",
	"taken": ["Good. I'll be right here. Probably.", "Thank you, Captain. Truly. Mind yourself out there.",
		"Ha! I knew you had the look. Go on, then.", "That's a weight off. Don't make me regret it.",
		"Off you go. I'll have something cold waiting when you're back.", "You're a good sort, for a pirate.",
		"Come back in one piece. I'm not paying for pieces.", "Done, then. I'll tell the others a captain's on it.",
		"Bless you. The spirits saw that. So did I.", "Right. Don't dawdle. The jungle doesn't wait.",
		"Wonderful. I'll start counting out your pay. Slowly."],
	# the village notice board: {name} the target, {poster} the villager who posted it (and whom you report to)
	"notices": {
		"board": ["A board of notices, curling and spotted with damp.", "Pages pinned up with fish-bone nails, half-eaten by bugs.",
			"Notices flap in the warm wind. Someone's scrawled a pig on one.", "A plank board under a little thatch roof, crowded with notes.",
			"Old notices peel beneath new ones. The ink runs in every rain.", "Bark-paper notices, weighted with shells, buzzing with flies."],
		"bounty": ["WANTED: {name}, who camps in our bush and robs our gardens. Bring proof to {poster}. Reward paid gladly.",
			"WANTED, alive or otherwise: {name}. Raider of canoes, drinker of our wine. Report to {poster}.",
			"{name} and their crew squat in the jungle like ticks. Drive them out and tell {poster}.",
			"REWARD for the end of {name}. They took our nets, our pigs and our patience. See {poster}.",
			"BY ORDER OF THE ELDER: {name} must go. Dangerous, loud, and owes the inn. Report to {poster}.",
			"Captain wanted to beat a captain. {name} holds the hills. Win, then see {poster} for pay."],
		"lair": ["HELP WANTED: {name} grows bigger every week. Clear it out and tell {poster}.",
			"The bugs from {name} are in the gardens again. Brave sorts, see {poster}.",
			"Clear {name} before the rains, and {poster} will pay in coin and wine.",
			"WANTED: someone with a strong arm and no sense. {name} needs emptying. Ask {poster}.",
			"Nobody sleeps for the humming from {name}. Silence it, then see {poster}.",
			"REWARD offered for clearing {name}. Bring word to {poster}, and bring back all your limbs."],
		"beast": ["BEAST WARNING: {name} walks the far side. Whoever brings it down, see {poster}. The whole village will pay.",
			"{name} smashed three huts and a canoe. Kill it, and {poster} will see you rewarded.",
			"WANTED: a hunter bigger than the hunted. {name} must fall. Report to {poster}.",
			"Our hunters won't go near {name}. If you will, and you live, tell {poster}.",
			"End {name} and the far side is ours again. {poster} keeps the reward safe till then.",
			"Tusks like masts, they say, on {name}. Any captain who ends it, report to {poster}."],
		"posted": ["It's done? Truly? I'll sleep tonight for the first time in a month.",
			"I'd heard captains were all talk. Not this one. Here's your due.",
			"The whole village owes you. I'll make sure they remember. Loudly.",
			"You've earned this, and a drink, and a song if the storyteller's sober.",
			"Done already? Then I'll take that notice down myself. With pleasure.",
			"Thank the spirits, and thank you. Mostly you. The spirits didn't do much.",
			"Look at you, still standing. Good. Here, before I start crying."],
	},
	# barks for the village's service folk
	"service": {
		"inn": ["Rooms are dry, mostly. Hammocks are free of bugs, mostly.",
			"Palm wine, fish stew, a hammock for the night. Pick two, or all three.",
			"Come in out of the rain. Or the sun. Whichever's trying to kill you today.",
			"Sit by the fire, Captain. Wet boots by the door, please.",
			"A captain's coin spends well here. A captain's stories spend better.",
			"Last pirate who started a brawl in here is now our doorstop.",
			"Bed for the night? Sleep well. The bugs will."],
		"trade": ["Buying and selling, Captain. Mostly selling. Mostly to you.",
			"Got loot? I've got coin. Let's make each other happy.",
			"Powder, shot, pepper and rope. Everything a pirate needs in the bush.",
			"Bring me what the pirates drop. I don't ask where it's been.",
			"Fair prices! Well. Fair for an island this far out.",
			"That trinket? Ugly. I'll take it. Ugly sells to sailors.",
			"Look around. If it's not here, the jungle ate it."],
		"cook": ["Fish stew, yam mash, roast pig. The pig was a friend. Eat up.",
			"Sit down and eat before you fall down. You look half-starved.",
			"Too much pepper? There's no such thing, Captain.",
			"Bring me fish and I'll make it sing. Bring me pork and I'll make it dance.",
			"Taste this. No, more. No, all of it. Good, yes?",
			"Coconut, lime and chilli. The jungle in one bowl.",
